{"id":76218,"title":"Volumetric Rendering using Path Tracing","url":"https://zydak.github.io/Clouds/index.html","final_url":"https://zydak.github.io/Clouds/index.html","year":null,"kind":"web","source":"ddg","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"a45830ad9e4e39bc212a6c152022d13fde393ce271bbf953387bcf418e8b17b0","ctype":"text/html; charset=utf-8","text_src":"url","fetched_at":1793141816.4206443,"text_chars":29717,"abstract":"zydak.github.io\n\nhttps://zydak.github.io › Clouds › index.html\n\nVolumetric Rendering using Path Tracing\nDec 7, 2025Free path lengths are sampled using this majorant coefficient, when an event occurs, an actual density at that point is evaluated, and based on that the decision is made whether the collision actually happened or if it's a null collision. If it's a null collision, sampling continues until an interaction is accepted or the ray exits the volume.","file":null,"marks":["unofficial"],"links":["https://zydak.github.io/Clouds/index.html"],"cited_by":[{"path":"985-nerf-training-loop-with-random-ray-batching.md","name":"NeRF Training Loop with Random Ray Batching","k":9},{"path":"1010-nerf-ray-generation.md","name":"NeRF Ray Generation","k":12},{"path":"1084-preprocessed-mesh-data-generation.md","name":"Preprocessed Mesh Data Generation","k":2},{"path":"985-delta-tracking.md","name":"Delta tracking","k":9},{"path":"1010-henyey-greenstein-phase-function.md","name":"Henyey-Greenstein Phase Function","k":12},{"path":"1044-ratio-tracking-with-null-scattering.md","name":"Ratio Tracking with Null Scattering","k":2},{"path":"1371-russian-roulette.md","name":"Russian Roulette","k":3},{"path":"1084-woodcock-tracking-with-variable-majorants.md","name":"Woodcock Tracking with Variable Majorants","k":2},{"path":"1338-biased-sampling-for-path-depth.md","name":"Biased Sampling for Path Depth","k":1},{"path":"980-homogeneous-medium-sampling.md","name":"Homogeneous Medium Sampling","k":5}]}